I've been playing nethack 3.0j for some time now, and I'd
really like to try 3.1.  Sadly, my machine is a clunky old
286 running at 10MHz with 640k, and the hard disk is _slow_
:-(  The upshot of this is that 3.1 is unplayable.  Every
step I take results in a second or so of disk access.  I
explored the first dungeon level, but it took forever, and
I thought my drive was going to explode!

My question: what's the cheapest way to fix this?  More
memory to reduce swapping?  How much would I need?
Obviously my slow drive is a bottleneck, but if I can fit
more of the program in memory then disk accesses should
be much less frequent.

Has anybody had similar experiences?  If so, I'd like to
hear about them.

By the way, having a slow system was actually helpful
sometimes in 3.0j.  If the game started slowing down, I'd
know that a lot of nasties had just been generated on the
level.  I don't know if you people with faster/better
computers could notice this.  Of course, throne rooms, zoos,
the castle etc. took some patience!

